# Coding Guidelines

- Clean, modular modules: separate SLA engine, inventory, and vendor scoring from UI
- Strict error handling + input validation on ticket create/update and SLA calculations
- Business constants (SLA hours, peak window, 99.9% target, 10% buffer) live in `config/` or Prisma models — never scattered literals
- UI: Operation Center style — dense KPIs, clear SLA badges (On Track / Warning / Breached), accessible contrast, dark/light toggle
- Prefer TypeScript end-to-end with Prisma types for Vendor, EdcUnit, Ticket, MetricLog
